### Project Files API Documentation
### Complete API documentation for project files management endpoints
### All operations for creating, updating, approving, and rejecting project files

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
@contentType = application/json
@token = your-jwt-token-here
@freelancerToken = your-freelancer-jwt-token-here
@clientToken = your-client-jwt-token-here
@projectFilesId = your-project-files-uuid-here
@projectId = your-project-uuid-here
@contractId = your-contract-uuid-here

### ============================================
### VARIABLES SETUP
### ============================================
### Replace the variables above with actual values:
### - @token: JWT token from /api/auth/verify-otp
### - @freelancerToken: JWT token for a freelancer user
### - @clientToken: JWT token for a client user
### - @projectFilesId: UUID of an existing project files record
### - @projectId: UUID of an existing project
### - @contractId: UUID of an existing contract

### ============================================
### 1. CREATE PROJECT FILES
### ============================================
### Create project files for a contract (requires authentication and freelancer role)
### Only the freelancer who created the proposal (and has the contract) can create project files
### Files require upload tokens from /api/s3/upload-url endpoint first
### Required fields: projectId, contractId
### Optional fields: files, notes

POST {{baseUrl}}/project-files
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{freelancerToken}}

{
  "projectId": "fbf62ddc-2136-43d6-911f-b062e606a808",
  "contractId": "cb2cf78f-2c0f-4698-a183-14b4f9d2f5a7",
  "files": [
    {
      "fileId": "770e8400-e29b-41d4-a716-446655440003",
      "token": "upload-token-from-s3-upload-url-endpoint",
      "purpose": "projectfiles"
    },
    {
      "fileId": "770e8400-e29b-41d4-a716-446655440004",
      "token": "upload-token-from-s3-upload-url-endpoint",
      "purpose": "projectfiles"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    {
      "text": "Initial project files submission",
      "createdAt": "2026-02-07T12:00:00.000Z"
    }
  ]
}

### Create Project Files Without Files (Optional)
POST {{baseUrl}}/project-files
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{freelancerToken}}

{
  "projectId": "fbf62ddc-2136-43d6-911f-b062e606a808",
  "contractId": "cb2cf78f-2c0f-4698-a183-14b4f9d2f5a7",
  "notes": []
}

### Create Project Files with Notes Only
POST {{baseUrl}}/project-files
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{freelancerToken}}

{
  "projectId": "fbf62ddc-2136-43d6-911f-b062e606a808",
  "contractId": "cb2cf78f-2c0f-4698-a183-14b4f9d2f5a7",
  "files": [],
  "notes": [
    {
      "text": "Project files will be uploaded soon",
      "createdAt": "2026-02-07T12:00:00.000Z"
    }
  ]
}

### ============================================
### 2. UPDATE PROJECT FILES
### ============================================
### Update project files (requires authentication and freelancer role)
### Only the freelancer who created the project files can update them
### Files require upload tokens from /api/s3/upload-url endpoint first
### At least one field must be provided: files or status
### All fields are optional - update only what you need

### Update Files Only
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/project-files/{{projectFilesId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{freelancerToken}}

{
  "files": [
    {
      "fileId": "770e8400-e29b-41d4-a716-446655440005",
      "token": "upload-token-from-s3-upload-url-endpoint",
      "purpose": "projectfiles"
    },
    {
      "fileId": "770e8400-e29b-41d4-a716-446655440006",
      "token": "upload-token-from-s3-upload-url-endpoint",
      "purpose": "projectfiles"
    }
  ]
}

### Update Status Only (Freelancer can reset to pending)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/project-files/{{projectFilesId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{freelancerToken}}

{
  "status": "pending"
}

### Update Both Files and Status
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/project-files/{{projectFilesId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{freelancerToken}}

{
  "files": [
    {
      "fileId": "770e8400-e29b-41d4-a716-446655440007",
      "token": "upload-token-from-s3-upload-url-endpoint",
      "purpose": "projectfiles"
    }
  ],
  "status": "pending"
}

### ============================================
### 3. ADD NOTES TO PROJECT FILES
### ============================================
### Add notes to project files (requires authentication and freelancer role)
### Only the freelancer who created the project files can add notes
### Notes are appended to the existing notes array
### At least one note is required

PATCH {{baseUrl}}/project-files/{{projectFilesId}}/notes
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{freelancerToken}}

{
  "notes": [
    {
      "text": "Updated project files with latest changes",
      "createdAt": "2026-02-07T14:00:00.000Z"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fixed bugs in the implementation",
      "createdAt": "2026-02-07T14:05:00.000Z"
    }
  ]
}

### Add Single Note
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/project-files/{{projectFilesId}}/notes
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{freelancerToken}}

{
  "notes": [
    {
      "text": "Project files updated",
      "createdAt": "2026-02-07T15:00:00.000Z"
    }
  ]
}

### ============================================
### 4. REJECT PROJECT FILES
### ============================================
### Reject project files (requires authentication and client role)
### Only the project owner (client) can reject project files
### Sets status to "rejected"
### No request body required

PATCH {{baseUrl}}/project-files/{{projectFilesId}}/reject
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{clientToken}}

### ============================================
### 5. APPROVE PROJECT FILES
### ============================================
### Approve project files (requires authentication and client role)
### Only the project owner (client) can approve project files
### Sets status to "approved"
### Automatically:
###   - Updates project status to "completed"
###   - Updates contract status to "completed"
###   - Releases escrow wallet funds to freelancer
###   - Transfers funds from escrow to freelancer's wallet
### No request body required

PATCH {{baseUrl}}/project-files/{{projectFilesId}}/approve
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{clientToken}}

### Approve with Optional Body (projectId and contractId are optional)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/project-files/{{projectFilesId}}/approve
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{clientToken}}

{
  "projectId": "fbf62ddc-2136-43d6-911f-b062e606a808",
  "contractId": "cb2cf78f-2c0f-4698-a183-14b4f9d2f5a7"
}

### ============================================
### COMPREHENSIVE NOTES & GUIDELINES
### ============================================

### 1. AUTHENTICATION & AUTHORIZATION
###    - All endpoints require JWT token in Authorization header
###    - Format: Authorization: Bearer <token>
###    - Get token from: POST /api/auth/verify-otp
###    
###    Freelancer-only endpoints (requires freelancer role):
###    - POST /api/project-files (create project files)
###    - PATCH /api/project-files/:id (update project files)
###    - PATCH /api/project-files/:id/notes (add notes)
###    
###    Client-only endpoints (requires client role):
###    - PATCH /api/project-files/:id/reject (reject project files)
###    - PATCH /api/project-files/:id/approve (approve project files)

### 2. FILE UPLOADS
###    - Files require upload tokens from /api/s3/upload-url endpoint first
###    - File purpose must be "projectfiles" for project files
###    - File format: [{ fileId: "uuid", token: "upload-token", purpose: "projectfiles" }]
###    - Files must be uploaded to S3 before they can be used
###    - Upload flow:
###      1. POST /api/s3/upload-url with filePurpose: "projectfiles"
###      2. Upload file to S3 using the returned uploadUrl
###      3. Use fileId and token in project files creation/update request

### 3. PROJECT FILES STATUS VALUES
###    - "pending" - Project files are pending review (default)
###    - "approved" - Project files have been approved by client
###    - "rejected" - Project files have been rejected by client

### 4. NOTES FORMAT
###    - Notes are stored as an array of objects
###    - Each note object can contain any fields (typically: text, createdAt)
###    - Notes are appended to existing notes when using add notes endpoint
###    - Example note structure:
###      {
###        "text": "Note content here",
###        "createdAt": "2026-02-07T12:00:00.000Z"
###      }

### 5. REQUIRED FIELDS FOR CREATE
###    - projectId: UUID (required, must exist in Projects table)
###    - contractId: UUID (required, must exist in Contracts table)
###    - files: Array of file references (optional, defaults to empty array)
###    - notes: Array of note objects (optional, defaults to empty array)

### 6. UPDATE PROJECT FILES
###    - Endpoint: PATCH /api/project-files/:id
###    - At least one field must be provided
###    - Editable fields:
###      * files: Array of file references with upload tokens
###      * status: Enum (pending, approved, rejected)
###    - Only the freelancer who created the project files can update them
###    - Returns 403 Forbidden if user is not the creator
###    - Returns 404 Not Found if project files don't exist

### 7. ADD NOTES TO PROJECT FILES
###    - Endpoint: PATCH /api/project-files/:id/notes
###    - At least one note is required
###    - Notes are appended to existing notes array
###    - Only the freelancer who created the project files can add notes
###    - Returns 403 Forbidden if user is not the creator
###    - Returns 404 Not Found if project files don't exist

### 8. REJECT PROJECT FILES
###    - Endpoint: PATCH /api/project-files/:id/reject
###    - No request body required
###    - Sets status to "rejected"
###    - Only the project owner (client) can reject project files
###    - Returns 403 Forbidden if user is not the project owner
###    - Returns 404 Not Found if project files don't exist

### 9. APPROVE PROJECT FILES
###    - Endpoint: PATCH /api/project-files/:id/approve
###    - No request body required (projectId and contractId are optional)
###    - Sets project files status to "approved"
###    - Automatically updates:
###      * Project status to "completed"
###      * Contract status to "completed"
###      * Releases escrow wallet funds to freelancer
###      * Transfers funds from escrow to freelancer's wallet
###    - Only the project owner (client) can approve project files
###    - Returns 403 Forbidden if user is not the project owner
###    - Returns 404 Not Found if project files don't exist
###    - Returns 400 Bad Request if escrow wallet or contract issues occur

### 10. DATA RELATIONSHIPS
###     - Project files belong to a Project (projectId)
###     - Project files belong to a Contract (contractId)
###     - Project files are created by a User (createdById - freelancer)
###     - Project files have multiple Files (files array of UUIDs)
###     - Project files have filesData (array of FileHub objects with full file details)
###     - Project files have notes (array of note objects)
###     - Contract must belong to the project (validated on creation)
###     - Only one project files record can exist per contract

### 11. AUTHORIZATION RULES
###     - CREATE: Only freelancer who created the proposal (and has the contract) can create
###     - UPDATE: Only freelancer who created the project files can update
###     - ADD NOTES: Only freelancer who created the project files can add notes
###     - REJECT: Only project owner (client) can reject
###     - APPROVE: Only project owner (client) can approve

### 12. VALIDATION RULES
###     - projectId must be a valid UUID and exist in Projects table
###     - contractId must be a valid UUID and exist in Contracts table
###     - Contract must belong to the project (validated)
###     - Only one project files record per contract (validated)
###     - Files must have valid upload tokens
###     - File purpose must be "projectfiles"

### 13. ERROR RESPONSES
###     - 400 Bad Request: Invalid input data, validation errors, or business logic errors
###     - 401 Unauthorized: Missing or invalid authentication token
###     - 403 Forbidden: User doesn't have required role or is not authorized
###     - 404 Not Found: Project files, project, or contract not found
###     - 500 Internal Server Error: Server error

### 14. EXAMPLE WORKFLOW
###     1. Authenticate: POST /api/auth/verify-otp (get token)
###     2. Create contract: POST /api/contracts (client creates contract)
###     3. Get upload URL: POST /api/s3/upload-url (freelancer gets upload URL)
###     4. Upload file to S3 using uploadUrl
###     5. Create project files: POST /api/project-files (freelancer submits files)
###     6. Add notes: PATCH /api/project-files/:id/notes (freelancer adds notes)
###     7. Update files: PATCH /api/project-files/:id (freelancer updates files)
###     8. (Client) Review and approve: PATCH /api/project-files/:id/approve
###        OR
###     (Client) Reject: PATCH /api/project-files/:id/reject

### 15. RESPONSE STRUCTURE
###     - All endpoints return: { success: boolean, message: string, data: object }
###     - Project files data includes:
###       * id: UUID
###       * projectId: UUID
###       * contractId: UUID
###       * createdById: UUID (freelancer who created)
###       * files: Array of file UUIDs
###       * filesData: Array of file objects with full details (id, url, fileName, etc.)
###       * notes: Array of note objects
###       * status: Enum (pending, approved, rejected)
###       * createdAt: DateTime
###       * updatedAt: DateTime

### 16. FILES DATA STRUCTURE
###     - filesData is automatically populated from files array
###     - Each file object contains:
###       * id: UUID
###       * url: String (file URL)
###       * fileName: String
###       * fileType: String
###       * filePurpose: String
###       * mimeType: String
###       * fileSize: Number
###       * status: String
###       * createdAt: DateTime
###       * updatedAt: DateTime

### 17. ESCROW WALLET RELEASE (On Approval)
###     - When project files are approved:
###       1. Escrow wallet balance is transferred to freelancer's wallet
###       2. Transaction is created to record the transfer
###       3. Project status is set to "completed"
###       4. Contract status is set to "completed"
###     - If escrow wallet or transaction fails, approval fails with error

### 18. NOTES ARRAY STRUCTURE
###     - Notes are stored as an array of objects
###     - Each note can have any structure (typically includes text and createdAt)
###     - Notes are appended when using add notes endpoint
###     - Example notes array:
###       [
###         {
###           "text": "Initial submission",
###           "createdAt": "2026-02-07T12:00:00.000Z"
###         },
###         {
###           "text": "Updated with fixes",
###           "createdAt": "2026-02-07T14:00:00.000Z"
###         }
###       ]
